      "text": "To find $\\cos 75^\\circ$, we can use the angle addition formula for cosine. We can express $75^\\circ$ as the sum of $45^\\circ$ and $30^\\circ$. So, we have:\n\n$$\\cos 75^\\circ = \\cos(45^\\circ + 30^\\circ)$$\n\nUsing the angle addition formula for cosine, we have:\n\n$$\\cos(45^\\circ + 30^\\circ) = \\cos 45^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ - \\sin 45^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ$$\n\nWe know that $\\cos 45^\\circ = \\sin 45^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$, $\\cos 30^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$, and $\\sin 30^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2}$. Substituting these values in, we get:\n\n$$\\cos 75^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}$$\n\nSimplifying, we have:\n\n$$\\cos 75^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} = \\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{2}}{4}}$$",
